---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import Button from "@components/Button.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Plugins & Client Mods"
  description="Use Shelter or Vencord with Legcord for Discord themes, custom CSS, and plugins. No injectors—enable in Legcord settings."
  canonical="/plugins"
>
  <article class="relative py-16 overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="plugins-heading">
    <div class="orb left-[-8%] top-[5%] h-[400px] w-[420px]" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(88,101,242,.2), transparent 70%);"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <header class="reveal visible text-center mb-10">
        <span class="eyebrow">Themes • CSS • Plugins</span>
        <h1 id="plugins-heading" class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white">
          <span class="text-gradient">Plugins & client mods</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-lg mt-4 mb-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Legcord supports <strong class="text-gray-200">client mods</strong> (plugins) that add Discord themes, custom CSS, and extra features. Enable or switch between them in <strong class="text-gray-200">Settings → Legcord</strong>. No separate installers or injectors are needed.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          Both <strong class="text-gray-400">Equicord</strong> and <strong class="text-gray-400">Vencord</strong> work with Legcord. Use one at a time to avoid conflicts. See the <a href="/faq" class="text-[#a5b4fc] hover:text-white link-underline">FAQ</a> for more on the difference between them.
        </p>
      </header>
      <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 text-center">Choose your client mod</h2>
      <div class="stagger grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-10">
        <Button name="Shelter" href="https://shelter.uwu.network/plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" description="Comes with every Legcord install" />
        <Button name="Vencord" href="https://vencord.dev/plugins#" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" description="Togglable in Legcord settings" />
        <Button name="Equicord" href="https://equicord.org/plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" description="Togglable in Legcord settings" />
      </div>
      <section class="reveal glass rounded-[22px] p-6 sm:p-8 relative overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="plugins-tips">
        <div class="absolute inset-x-10 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#818cf8]/60 to-transparent"></div>
        <h2 id="plugins-tips" class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white mb-4">Tips for using Discord plugins with Legcord</h2>
        <ul class="text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-2.5">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition">
            <span class="grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-[#5865f2]/25 text-[#a5b4fc] text-[11px] mt-0.5">›</span>
            Shelter is the default client mod and is recommended for most users.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition">
            <span class="grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-[#5865f2]/25 text-[#a5b4fc] text-[11px] mt-0.5">›</span>
            Themes and plugins are managed inside each mod's own settings or plugin list.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition">
            <span class="grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-[#5865f2]/25 text-[#a5b4fc] text-[11px] mt-0.5">›</span>
            Legcord developers are not affiliated with Shelter or Vencord. Only Shelter is officially supported with Legcord.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition">
            <span class="grid h-5 w-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-[#5865f2]/25 text-[#a5b4fc] text-[11px] mt-0.5">›</span>
            If something breaks after adding a plugin, try disabling it or switching mods.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
